From fdab6479c674541c396b0eb60285bd741da2c1ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Chatelain <ben@octop.ad>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:13:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(harness): add grok to the shared agent harness

- Move grok from the Homebrew cask grok-build onto mise
  (grok = "1.0.4" in .config/mise/config.toml); brew cask uninstalled
  without --zap to preserve the harness config generated at ~/.grok
- Register grok in scripts/agent-harnesses.py: HARNESSES,
  HARNESS_LABELS, ATTRIBUTE_MAPPINGS, and five new renderers
  (render_grok_config/rules/agent/hooks/guard) wired into render_all,
  GENERATED_ITEM_ROOTS, command_validate/verify/audit, and every
  build_manifest feature/parity table
- Extract COMPACTION_PRESERVATION as a shared constant so grok and omp
  cannot drift; render_omp_append_system output is byte-identical
- Give grok its own PreToolUse guard (~/.grok/hooks/harness-guard.json
  + scripts/harness-guard.py) that maps grok's camelCase hook payload
  onto the shared guard CLI, with Claude/Cursor native hook compat
  disabled in the generated config.toml since it can't parse grok's
  snake_case-free envelope
- Protect grok credentials (auth.json, mcp_credentials.json) in
  safety.py PROTECTED_PATHS and the generated safety-policy.json
- Append a Git Commit Attribution section to the generated grok rules
  file (Co-Authored-By: grokkybara[bot]) since grok has no native
  commit_attribution config key like Codex
- Allowlist .grok/{agents,config.toml,hooks,rules,scripts} in
  .gitignore and register .grok in audit-ignored-config.py
  HARNESS_ROOTS
- Add bats coverage: grok artifacts/parse test, guard wrapper camelCase
  mapping test, and grok added to every cross-harness guard loop and
  the documented-protected-paths test
- Regenerate harness artifacts: README.md, generated-paths.json,
  safety-policy.json, docs/agent-harnesses.{json,md}

Co-Authored-By: oh-my-pi <omp@can.ac>
